  "report": "# Dixon mixed two-jet and second-order path port\n\nDate: 2026-10-10. Status: AUTHOR_DERIVATION / FINITE_EXACT_CHECKS / UNREVIEWED / NOT_ADMITTED.\nAuthor: local logical conversation em-research2-20261010-743915c4a185. Registration request r2-20261010-session-03, bridge Issue 3572, remains pending at preparation. No service-issued Researcher identity, CLAIM, run, independent review or mathematical acceptance is asserted.\n\n## Question and source scope\n\nFor the finite terminating family F_m(a,d)=sum_{j=0}^m [(-m)_j/(d)_j] a/(a+j), extend the existing normal two-jet to simultaneous tangent/normal parameter motion and a second-order transverse path change. This is neutral supplemental research under the user's continuing research objective, not execution of an assigned Task. The latest admitted LOW frontier and winning owner have not yet been established by the pending research dispatcher.\n\nExact inputs consumed:\n- enterprise-math@73f10bca40f9f9d700f61e7cd0ad11391235ca61:research_notes/directed_recovery/20260926_13C1B7/math/D25_LOCAL_PROGRESS.md, blob 51dd15a8142f3dda0506a306f9c0693a036f5891.\n- enterprise-math@f73f2697a657858328492166b21fc2329264e05b:research_notes/portable_supplemental/20261010_R1_DIXON_P3_NORMALIZATION_54068cda.json, blob ef11be117e67a163d7b54e2dcf3f15de4289eda6.\nBoth inputs retain their UNREVIEWED / NOT_ADMITTED status. Their normal-displacement proof and 28-prime scan are consumed, not claimed as this author's new results or repeated unchanged.\n\n## Exact mixed-jet identity\n\nUse external algebraic parameter coordinates G(a,b)=F_m(a,m+a+1+b); these are not native spatial coordinates or a P000 plane. On b=0 let C(a)=G(a,0), N(a)=G_b(a,0), K(a)=G_bb(a,0). Prime denotes differentiation along this line. Therefore G_a=C', G_aa=C'', G_ab=N'.\n\nWrite B_j=(-m)_j/(m+a+1)_j, t_j=B_j*a/(a+j), H_j=sum_{l=0}^{j-1}1/(m+a+1+l), H2_j=sum_{l=0}^{j-1}1/(m+a+1+l)^2. Then\n\nN=-sum_j t_j H_j,\nK=sum_j t_j(H_j^2+H2_j),\nF_ad=-sum_j B_j*j*H_j/(a+j)^2,\nF_aa=-2 sum_j B_j*j/(a+j)^3,\nN'=F_ad+K,\nC''=F_aa+2F_ad+K.\n\nThese identities follow by differentiating each finite rational term. The closed C(a)=1+a sum_{r=0}^{m-1}[1/(a+2r+2)-1/(a+2r+1)] gives C' and C'' explicitly; it does not by itself give N'. Thus the mixed port has a concrete harmonic double-pole moment representation.\n\nSet p=6m+1 prime, p>=7, a=-1/3 and d=m+2/3. For integers alpha,beta,gamma define\n\nS(alpha,beta,gamma)=F_m(a+p*alpha,d+p*(alpha+beta)+p^2*gamma).\nL=alpha*C'+beta*N,\nQ=alpha^2*C''/2+alpha*beta*N'+beta^2*K/2+gamma*N.\n\nThen the all-admissible-prime finite algebra identity is\n\nS-C = p*L+p^2*Q (mod p^3).\n\nProof: all basepoint denominator factors are p-units, as established in the input's finite-family argument. Integer parameter shifts preserve their residues and hence this property. Each inverse factor admits the finite geometric expansion 1/(u+v)=1/u-v/u^2+v^2/u^3 mod p^3 for v in p Z_(p); the exact remainder has a factor v^3 and a p-unit denominator. Multiplying the finitely many factors and the rational numerator produces the two-variable formal jet. The coefficient of p is G_a*alpha+G_b*beta; the coefficient of p^2 is G_aa*alpha^2/2+G_ab*alpha*beta+G_bb*beta^2/2+G_b*gamma. Summing terms gives the formula. This proof uses finite rational algebra, not analytic convergence or inference from a prime scan.\n\n## Exact criterion for eliminating the normal ports\n\nThe tangent comparator is T=C(a+p*alpha). Define R=gamma*N+alpha*beta*N'+beta^2*K/2. Subtracting its own finite jet yields\n\nS-T = p*beta*N+p^2*R (mod p^3).\n\nConsequently S=T mod p^3 if and only if beta*N+p*R=0 mod p^2. The weaker mod p^2 condition is beta*N=0 mod p. Actual cancellation must be checked at the stated precision. A first-order tangent label beta=0 is insufficient for mod p^3 when gamma*N is nonzero mod p.\n\nFor beta=-2*alpha, the standalone K coefficient in alpha*beta*N'+beta^2*K/2 cancels after using N'=F_ad+K, but the remaining -2*alpha^2*F_ad need not vanish. Cancelling one Hessian coefficient is not proof of cancelling the mixed port.\n\n## New exact witnesses\n\nAt p=13, m=2, the exact jets give N=11, N'=6, K=3 and C''=0 modulo 13.\n\n1. Paths (alpha,beta,gamma)=(1,0,0) and (1,0,1) have the same first-order direction and first divided digit. Their values differ by p^2*N=1859 modulo p^3=2197. The latter is therefore not the closed tangent value through p^3. A path's first jet alone does not determine its second-order readout.\n2. At (1,-2,0), the normal quadratic correction is -2*6+2*3=7 mod13, even though the standalone K coefficient cancels as described above. Thus that shortcut still loses a nonzero harmonic mixed contribution.\n3. At (1,1,0), L mod169=82, its canonical first digit is 4 and carry is 6. Q mod13=1, so the canonical second divided digit is 7. The mixed correction cannot be replaced by the tangent C'' value, which is 0 mod13.\n\n## Carry, lifts and sufficient retained state\n\nD=(S-C)/p mod p^2 equals L+p*Q. Let ell=L mod p^2 be its least nonnegative representative, r=ell mod p, and c=(ell-r)/p. Then the canonical second digit of D is c+Q mod p. This composes the previous normal carry law with the actual mixed direction and second-order path port.\n\nThe scoped sufficient data are L mod p^2 and Q mod p, plus the declared path and digit convention. Before evaluating a family of directions, retain C',N mod p^2 and C'',N',K mod p together with alpha,beta modulo p^2 and gamma modulo p; exact source basepoint and m remain specified. This is sufficiency for this observer, not a global minimality claim. A change of the lift L to L+p*u changes a normal-subtracted second digit by -u; a simultaneous representation change Q to Q-u preserves D. Neither independent deletion of carry nor deletion of path curvature is licensed.\n\n## Actual BRC reuse and boundaries\n\nREUSE_APPLIED: the source F_m derivative interface and typed BRC carrier/observer discipline. Retain finite labels j, signed rational term we